WEBVTT

00:05.620 --> 00:07.150
There's no one here.

00:08.560 --> 00:09.610
They vanished?

00:10.010 --> 00:11.180
<i>The following morning,</i>

00:11.520 --> 00:13.650
<i>in the pool of the waterfall near the village,</i>

00:13.650 --> 00:16.090
<i>they found the official 
dead of unnatural causes.</i>

00:16.580 --> 00:21.080
<i>On his neck was bruising
that resembled the scales of a snake.</i>

00:21.920 --> 00:23.580
Detective Isshiki...

00:23.580 --> 00:27.670
your expression says that you've seen
through Yadagami's disappearing act.

00:27.670 --> 00:31.760
Living legends are created by the living.

00:46.190 --> 00:49.510
Ron    Kamonohashi's

00:46.190 --> 00:49.510
<i>Forbidden\h\h\h
</i>Deductions

02:04.060 --> 02:09.320
<b>#13   The Case of the Yadagami-sama Murders (Part 2)</b>

02:06.130 --> 02:09.310
Thank you all for gathering here.

02:09.310 --> 02:13.530
I'd now like to explain the murder 
that occurred in your village.

02:16.530 --> 02:21.480
Last night, after we saw Yadagami-sama 
and rushed over to the guest hut,

02:21.480 --> 02:25.250
this man accidentally dropped
his black sugar syrup on the floor.

02:25.250 --> 02:27.910
However, when we went to the guest hut today,

02:27.910 --> 02:30.580
the bottle was some distance from the spill.

02:31.210 --> 02:35.930
This man said he saw a white snake 
in the river, and when we investigated,

02:35.930 --> 02:38.630
we found a stone with a rope tied to it.

02:41.840 --> 02:45.630
These facts, the banging noise 
we heard when we entered the hut,

02:44.690 --> 02:51.150
<b>Temporarily
Closed</b>

02:45.630 --> 02:47.440
and the closure of the shrine...

02:47.440 --> 02:51.150
were the keys to Yadagami-sama's
 disappearing trick.

02:51.520 --> 02:52.860
Trick, you say?

02:52.860 --> 02:56.070
Yes. The Yadagami-sama we saw...

02:56.810 --> 02:59.530
was a painted scroll affixed to a tatami mat.

02:59.530 --> 03:00.740
What?!

03:04.120 --> 03:05.980
The culprit stood the mat upright,

03:05.980 --> 03:08.910
stuck the Yadagami-sama scroll to the back,

03:08.910 --> 03:10.680
and used the rope to hold it up.

03:10.680 --> 03:13.370
One end of the rope was shut in the door,

03:13.370 --> 03:17.340
while the other was tied to a rock 
hanging outside the window.

03:17.340 --> 03:21.800
So the moment we opened the door, 
the rope was freed,

03:21.800 --> 03:25.080
and the stone at the other end
plummeted into the river with it.

03:25.720 --> 03:27.340
The mat then fell back into place,

03:27.340 --> 03:29.030
as if nothing had ever happened.

03:29.740 --> 03:33.190
The bang we heard was just 
the mat falling back to the floor.

03:33.190 --> 03:35.650
Th-That's the truth behind
Yadagami's disappearance?

03:35.650 --> 03:39.110
I'm certain this old painting 
is what we saw that night.

03:41.450 --> 03:44.390
The reason the bottle 
rolled away from the stain

03:44.390 --> 03:48.750
is because the culprit had lifted 
the mat to retrieve the scroll.

03:49.370 --> 03:51.710
But... who would do such a thing?

03:51.710 --> 03:54.840
The culprit didn't want the villagers 
to be accused of the crime,

03:54.840 --> 03:56.920
so they planned it to seem impossible.

03:57.230 --> 04:00.160
For their trick to work, 
they needed someone to witness it.

04:00.880 --> 04:03.340
And the person who led us to our room...

04:03.340 --> 04:05.430
was you, Mayor, wasn't it?

04:08.680 --> 04:11.530
Wh-What's this all of a sudden?

04:11.530 --> 04:12.970
Now, as for this morning...

04:12.970 --> 04:15.570
The corpse showed bruising
resembling snakeskin,

04:15.570 --> 04:18.980
and we mentioned the person we'd seen
 constricted by a snake the night before.

04:18.980 --> 04:22.200
Normally, one's first thought 
would be of the victim,

04:22.510 --> 04:25.280
but you immediately declared
 it had been the Yadagami!

04:25.280 --> 04:28.990
Because you knew we'd seen that scroll!

04:28.990 --> 04:31.710
Th-That doesn't amount to evidence!

04:32.100 --> 04:34.920
First of all, no one's found 
the murder weapon! Where is it?

04:36.970 --> 04:41.190
I-It's true the weapon 
would be your link to the body...

04:41.190 --> 04:43.560
Brilliant, Detective Isshiki! The ligature!

04:43.560 --> 04:45.640
Uh, I said the link?

04:45.640 --> 04:48.390
You must mean the rope tied to the shrine.

04:49.390 --> 04:50.600
Huh?

04:50.600 --> 04:54.250
Looking closely, I can see it's
 tied differently than it was yesterday,

04:54.250 --> 04:57.260
as though it was used for something
 and then returned.

04:57.560 --> 04:59.020
<i>I get it now!</i>

04:59.380 --> 05:01.730
The murder weapon was the shrine rope!

05:01.730 --> 05:04.260
Once we investigate, we'll find skin cells

05:04.260 --> 05:06.740
from both the victim <i>and</i> you on it!

05:15.710 --> 05:18.690
Th-That can't be! I mean—

05:18.690 --> 05:21.380
Mii, it's all right.

05:21.760 --> 05:22.840
Grandpa...

05:22.840 --> 05:26.480
I'm sorry, Mii, everyone.

05:29.300 --> 05:31.620
I did it.

05:32.290 --> 05:35.830
I hated the official who
 came wanting to build the dam,

05:35.830 --> 05:39.170
so I called him out here and killed him.

05:39.170 --> 05:42.730
Is that truly the only reason?

05:42.730 --> 05:45.450
Isn't there something else you're hiding?

05:52.650 --> 05:54.060
Fall.

05:54.790 --> 05:56.000
<i>Here it comes!</i>

05:56.310 --> 05:59.370
Console the dead with your own death.

06:00.210 --> 06:02.670
Wh-What are you saying?

06:02.670 --> 06:04.630
Fall into the waterfall.

06:07.090 --> 06:08.890
All right. I will.

06:15.610 --> 06:18.970
Fall... Fall...

06:18.970 --> 06:20.430
Fall...

06:24.110 --> 06:25.070
Don't!

06:25.070 --> 06:26.400
Come back to your senses!

06:29.350 --> 06:31.660
What was I...

06:34.330 --> 06:37.000
You're all right now. Don't worry.

06:50.180 --> 06:51.170
Grandpa!

06:51.170 --> 06:51.890
Tototo!

07:01.430 --> 07:02.480
Are those two okay?!

07:02.480 --> 07:05.150
Hurry! Get something!
It doesn't matter what!

07:11.950 --> 07:14.150
Mayor, please grab hold!

07:15.620 --> 07:16.840
We'll pull you up! Hang on!

07:16.840 --> 07:18.030
I'll help, too!

07:30.970 --> 07:35.720
Mii, please find happiness.

07:36.350 --> 07:37.930
Grandpa...

07:37.930 --> 07:39.600
Let's go, Mayor.

08:00.620 --> 08:02.960
How about you come out now?

08:03.350 --> 08:05.920
You're the one who threw 
the rope, aren't you?

08:14.080 --> 08:16.640
You sure have grown up, Spitz.

08:16.640 --> 08:18.600
B-Big Brother?

08:18.600 --> 08:22.060
When did you two realize I was here?

08:22.430 --> 08:23.560
Toto.

08:23.560 --> 08:24.520
Right.

08:24.520 --> 08:26.970
When Muroi said he'd passed out
 in the wilderness

08:26.970 --> 08:29.390
and woken up at the base of the mountain,

08:29.390 --> 08:33.240
we considered that someone living
on the mountain had rescued him.

08:33.240 --> 08:36.620
Then we remembered that when
 Mii-san went to make an offering,

08:36.620 --> 08:39.090
she had an insulated bag with her.

08:42.050 --> 08:45.380
We figured she might be leaving food
for someone on the mountain.

08:45.380 --> 08:47.840
And there was also...

08:48.430 --> 08:52.750
When Mii saw Spitz, she blurted, 
"Why are you here?"

08:52.750 --> 08:57.850
We had to wonder if the person 
she'd been feeding looked like Spitz.

08:57.850 --> 09:01.060
So we thought, just maybe,
they were brothers.

09:01.470 --> 09:03.590
Right, Detective Isshiki?

09:03.590 --> 09:04.560
Yup, yup.

09:05.020 --> 09:06.600
I see.

09:06.600 --> 09:09.480
You've made yourself some good, 
talented friends here, Spitz.

09:11.580 --> 09:13.900
Why'd you disappear on me like that?!

09:16.840 --> 09:18.700
It all started fifteen years ago...

09:19.360 --> 09:22.220
While I was visiting this village on research,

09:22.650 --> 09:25.570
the mayor told me 
about the plans to build a dam.

09:25.570 --> 09:29.030
I suggested that he use the legends 
of Yadagami to play a trick.

09:29.030 --> 09:30.950
I was only kidding.

09:31.510 --> 09:33.870
But after I returned to my country,

09:33.870 --> 09:36.810
I learned he'd hidden 
the heavy machinery in the mountains

09:36.810 --> 09:39.310
and stymied the dam construction.

09:40.440 --> 09:44.560
Then, four years later, while I was
 doing fieldwork in another country,

09:44.560 --> 09:46.760
my life changed completely.

09:48.010 --> 09:50.560
I learned something I never should have,

09:50.560 --> 09:53.240
which caused a certain organization 
to come after me.

09:54.440 --> 09:56.150
Who're you talking about?

09:56.150 --> 09:58.480
Even on pain of death, I'll never tell.

09:58.480 --> 10:01.870
If I did, I couldn't promise
 safety for either of you.

10:04.070 --> 10:08.780
That's the reason you went missing 
without informing your family, isn't it?

10:09.130 --> 10:10.750
Yes, it is.

10:10.750 --> 10:13.900
After I evaded my pursuers 
and eventually drifted here,

10:13.900 --> 10:17.520
I took advantage of the village's gratitude
for my part in forestalling the dam

10:17.520 --> 10:19.910
and took shelter in the mountains.

10:19.910 --> 10:22.890
So the villagers know you're here?

10:22.890 --> 10:26.660
Yes, ever since the day 
I disappeared and left Spitz.

10:26.660 --> 10:28.230
So that's the deal...

10:28.230 --> 10:30.690
The whole village conspired to hide you.

10:30.690 --> 10:34.300
But in the end, 
I brought misfortune on these people.

10:34.710 --> 10:39.050
It was because of me 
that the mayor killed that official.

10:42.550 --> 10:44.830
The official discovered I was here

10:44.830 --> 10:46.760
and realized there must
 be unusual circumstances,

10:46.760 --> 10:50.320
so he demanded money in exchange 
for keeping our secret.

10:50.660 --> 10:52.720
Before long, his demands escalated.

10:52.720 --> 10:55.590
When he threatened 
to expose me to the world...

10:55.860 --> 10:57.550
that's when tragedy struck.

10:58.050 --> 10:59.010
I see.

10:59.540 --> 11:01.100
I had no idea.

11:01.630 --> 11:02.970
Grandpa...

11:03.490 --> 11:06.810
I don't intend to live at the 
expense of others' happiness.

11:06.810 --> 11:10.150
Isshiki-kun, was it? You should arrest me.

11:10.150 --> 11:11.150
What?

11:11.150 --> 11:12.110
You can't!

11:12.110 --> 11:15.080
Big Brother! I just found 
you again after so long!

11:15.080 --> 11:16.450
Spitz...

11:16.450 --> 11:20.280
I just wanted to tell you the truth 
of the incident before I was caught.

11:20.810 --> 11:22.170
Now, Isshiki-kun,

11:22.580 --> 11:24.390
there's instigating the 
concealment of heavy machinery

11:24.390 --> 11:26.240
and much more to charge me with.

11:26.240 --> 11:27.880
Big Brother, wait!

11:27.880 --> 11:31.460
Was the mayor really trying to protect you?

11:32.670 --> 11:35.390
This is just conjecture on my part,

11:35.390 --> 11:37.880
but I think what he truly wanted to protect...

11:38.160 --> 11:41.340
were Mii-kun's feelings for you.

11:45.510 --> 11:47.050
Mii...

11:47.050 --> 11:48.980
Even for a man like me, you...

11:54.900 --> 11:59.890
We're the ones who dragged out the man 
Yadagami-sama had stolen away.

12:00.300 --> 12:03.620
I'm sure divine wrath is in store. 
Yadagami-sama's rage will descend.

12:03.620 --> 12:07.330
That's when the heavens open up, isn't it?

12:09.290 --> 12:12.500
I'd rather not get soaked to the bone.
 I'm heading home.

12:12.500 --> 12:15.960
Hold on! I thought you 
didn't believe in the occult.

12:22.340 --> 12:26.100
As this case has now been solved, 
I will take my leave as well.

12:27.810 --> 12:28.930
Wait up!

12:44.120 --> 12:47.860
<i>Thank you, Tototo, Ron-kun!</i>

13:07.560 --> 13:09.080
<i>Now it's my turn!</i>

13:09.080 --> 13:10.810
<i>Just you wait, Ron-kun!</i>

13:10.810 --> 13:15.340
<i>Ron-kun couldn't have murdered anyone 
in the Bloody Training Incident.</i>

13:15.770 --> 13:19.270
<i>What truths are held within 
the file sleeping here?</i>

13:19.270 --> 13:20.540
That's far enough.

13:21.930 --> 13:24.660
Could this be what you're looking for,

13:25.030 --> 13:26.870
Instructor Spitz Fire?

13:28.580 --> 13:30.170
Principal?

13:30.980 --> 13:34.520
Trying to steal Kamonohashi 
Ron's incident file...

13:34.520 --> 13:37.000
I trust you are prepared 
for the consequences!

13:38.710 --> 13:41.520
Of course! I owe him so much.

13:41.520 --> 13:43.380
Come what may, I regret nothing!

13:51.510 --> 13:54.420
In that case, I have a favor to ask of you.

13:54.420 --> 13:55.480
What?

14:02.320 --> 14:04.490
Ron-kun, I'm back!

14:04.490 --> 14:06.200
Welcome, Spitz!

14:06.200 --> 14:07.750
I'm glad to see you're okay.

14:08.400 --> 14:09.710
Thanks, Tototo!

14:10.110 --> 14:12.460
So, do you have the file?

14:12.460 --> 14:14.730
<i>He's stiff with nerves.</i>

14:15.550 --> 14:17.220
About that...

14:21.110 --> 14:22.470
It wasn't there.

14:22.470 --> 14:23.470
What?

14:24.630 --> 14:26.430
I thought that might be the case.

14:26.430 --> 14:28.680
But I do have a message for you.

14:28.680 --> 14:32.170
It's important, so the principal 
asked me to make sure you get it.

14:33.370 --> 14:36.400
The message is on this tablet.

14:36.400 --> 14:40.110
But it'll disappear once opened, 
so she said to be careful.

14:41.180 --> 14:42.620
Let me read it.

14:49.700 --> 14:51.300
It's a cipher.

14:51.710 --> 14:53.820
I'll be able to crack this quickly.

14:53.820 --> 14:56.970
We don't want to get in your way, 
so we'll be over there.

14:56.970 --> 14:58.170
Wait.

14:59.880 --> 15:03.840
It's asking for a password made up 
of personal information from you two.

15:03.840 --> 15:05.030
What?

15:09.300 --> 15:11.320
It's a message for you, isn't it?

15:11.320 --> 15:13.290
Is it okay for us to hear it, too?

15:13.290 --> 15:15.530
The reason I need you two for the password

15:15.530 --> 15:17.870
is because she wanted you to hear it, too.

15:17.870 --> 15:18.730
I'll read it.

15:21.380 --> 15:24.680
"The situation is dire, Kamonohashi Ron,

15:24.680 --> 15:27.660
so I will now tell you the truth."

15:27.960 --> 15:31.770
"The clues you seek about 
the Bloody Training Incident..."

15:31.770 --> 15:35.630
<i>...have already been erased 
from both the police's files and BLUE's.</i>

15:35.630 --> 15:37.950
<i>Concerning the incident,</i>

15:37.950 --> 15:40.820
<i>a bloodstain that was neither 
yours nor the victims',</i>

15:40.820 --> 15:45.050
<i>but from someone else entirely 
was found at the scene.</i>

15:45.630 --> 15:48.190
<i>Yet none could solve 
the mystery of the locked room</i>

15:48.190 --> 15:50.150
<i>where the murders took place,</i>

15:50.150 --> 15:53.610
<i>so no one could clear your name of suspicion.</i>

15:54.270 --> 16:01.480
<i>At some point, someone erased the data 
on the unknown blood from all of the files.</i>

16:03.440 --> 16:08.110
<i>Then Instructor Grizzly was killed 
in the observatory case,</i>

16:08.110 --> 16:13.450
<i>and there was a report of a mark matching 
the one on your neck left at the scene.</i>

16:13.450 --> 16:16.470
<i>I became convinced of something.</i>

16:16.920 --> 16:21.300
<i>The incident five years ago was 
committed by a certain organization,</i>

16:21.300 --> 16:23.380
<i>and you were falsely accused.</i>

16:24.070 --> 16:27.420
<i>That mark that appeared on your
 neck later, during treatment,</i>

16:27.420 --> 16:32.350
<i>was likely inflicted at the same time
as your culprit-killing disorder.</i>

16:32.350 --> 16:36.560
<i>There's only one organization 
in the world capable of such a thing...</i>

16:39.190 --> 16:40.510
<i>The House of M!</i>

16:40.510 --> 16:42.190
What? Of all things!

16:42.190 --> 16:43.900
What's the House of M?

16:46.790 --> 16:50.020
It's said that all crime passes
 through the House of M.

16:50.020 --> 16:53.080
And what they commit themselves
 is guaranteed to go unsolved.

16:53.080 --> 16:55.830
They're the most heinous 
criminal family in history.

16:55.830 --> 17:01.170
There's a handful of cases that even the most
accomplished BLUE alumni have yet to solve.

17:01.170 --> 17:04.850
It's said the House of M is involved 
with 90 percent of them.

17:04.850 --> 17:07.800
An organization like that's after Ron?

17:09.510 --> 17:12.390
Ron-kun, read us the rest.

17:14.470 --> 17:18.100
"I would like to uncover the truth 
underlying these things,

17:18.100 --> 17:22.520
but as I've learned there is a mole from
the House of M within BLUE,

17:22.520 --> 17:24.690
I must act with the utmost caution."

17:24.690 --> 17:26.480
There's a spy in the school?!

17:26.480 --> 17:32.160
"That is why I had no choice but to send 
a message to you in this manner."

17:32.160 --> 17:35.380
"I hold your abilities in high esteem."

17:35.380 --> 17:37.960
"One day, when you've 
proven your innocence,

17:37.960 --> 17:41.710
I look forward to reinstating 
your detective's license."

17:41.710 --> 17:46.320
<i>Ron, your parents and I were old friends.</i>

17:46.320 --> 17:49.320
<i>I've watched over you since you were born.</i>

17:49.700 --> 17:54.930
<i>When I heard that you'd made 
trustworthy friends, I was overjoyed.</i>

17:54.930 --> 17:57.140
<i>Isshiki Totomaru-san,</i>

17:57.140 --> 17:59.120
<i>Instructor Spitz...</i>

17:59.600 --> 18:02.550
<i>Please look after Ron for me.</i>

18:03.060 --> 18:05.160
"Be very careful."

18:05.160 --> 18:08.330
Signed Emé Emmerich, Principal of BLUE.

18:14.550 --> 18:18.170
Now we know who framed Ron.

18:18.170 --> 18:22.250
Let's catch these House of M guys 
and make them tell us everything about Ron!

18:22.250 --> 18:25.080
Tototo... I love your determination,

18:25.080 --> 18:27.710
but it won't mean anything
 against these people.

18:27.710 --> 18:30.480
The BLUE alumni who've tried
 to crack the cases

18:30.480 --> 18:32.980
that the House of M was involved in

18:32.980 --> 18:34.930
have all died mysterious deaths.

18:35.460 --> 18:37.020
You mean they were killed?

18:37.520 --> 18:40.150
The truth is shrouded in darkness.

18:40.850 --> 18:43.480
A group that dangerous is...

18:45.030 --> 18:46.430
Ron.

18:59.120 --> 19:01.580
Well, this is a problem.

19:02.040 --> 19:05.790
I'm so excited that I can't stop trembling.

19:09.630 --> 19:15.660
As long as Toto and I keep solving cases, 
they're sure to show themselves again.

19:16.600 --> 19:19.310
But next time, we won't let them slip away.

19:21.710 --> 19:24.970
We'll drag the House of M into the light!

21:00.410 --> 21:01.830
Big Brother.

21:01.830 --> 21:06.660
Chris, the Ripper killer, is going to 
have a baby and would like to go straight.

21:06.990 --> 21:08.740
So we've got an issue.

21:08.740 --> 21:11.590
I'll have him ripped to shreds
 and get someone new.

21:11.590 --> 21:13.940
That's not a bad idea,

21:13.940 --> 21:17.380
but it could give rise to someone bent 
on revenge fifteen years from now.

21:18.380 --> 21:21.390
Make sure you pull the tiniest 
sprouts out by the roots, too.

21:21.390 --> 21:23.140
Of course.

21:23.510 --> 21:26.470
Why has an organization 
as meticulous as ours

21:26.470 --> 21:28.980
allowed that half-blood to live?

21:28.980 --> 21:30.630
Hey, Winter!

21:30.630 --> 21:33.020
That's no way to talk to our big brother!

21:34.400 --> 21:36.740
Do you mean Kamonohashi Ron?

21:37.280 --> 21:38.910
Who else could I mean?

21:38.910 --> 21:42.970
It's because he's part of the family.
He carries the same blood we do.

21:42.970 --> 21:44.280
Family?

21:44.280 --> 21:45.960
Then what about Alice?

21:45.960 --> 21:47.990
She shared our blood too!

21:47.990 --> 21:49.820
I wasn't finished.

21:49.820 --> 21:53.000
To be precise,
only those who excel will remain.

21:53.000 --> 21:56.070
Will Kamonohashi Ron prove 
worthy of being our brother?

21:56.070 --> 21:57.970
That's what we're trying to determine.

21:57.970 --> 22:01.050
But he carries the blood 
of Sherlock Holmes, too!

22:01.050 --> 22:02.890
He'll never be <i>my</i> brother.

22:06.890 --> 22:08.810
Winter.

22:08.810 --> 22:12.270
Are you still angry about the fact 
that we disposed of Alice?

22:13.480 --> 22:14.600
Let go of me!

22:14.600 --> 22:15.690
W-Wait!

22:16.840 --> 22:22.950
There is but one way to fulfill
both your desires and mine.

22:25.120 --> 22:26.970
Despair.

22:27.800 --> 22:30.900
The House of M's perfect crimes

22:30.900 --> 22:36.640
have long been foiled by Sherlock 
Holmes and his descendants.

22:37.300 --> 22:42.910
Kamonohashi Ron carries his blood, 
so the one thing we cannot allow

22:42.910 --> 22:44.730
is him to become a detective.

22:47.970 --> 22:50.750
Therefore, we shall bestow despair upon him.

22:51.200 --> 22:55.470
We will ascertain whether he 
is worthy of the House of Moriarty

22:55.470 --> 22:58.670
after he has completely 
given up on his deductions.

22:59.360 --> 23:02.620
Even if he becomes incapacitated 
in the process, so be it.

23:04.720 --> 23:08.130
It would simply mean that 
that's all he was capable of.

23:12.960 --> 23:15.170
I will be <i>very</i> thorough.

23:17.630 --> 23:19.460
I'm counting on it.

23:19.170 --> 23:22.840
<b>First-Born of the Moriarty Family
Milo Moriarty</b>

23:19.900 --> 23:22.840
There's a ticket to Japan waiting for you.

23:23.120 --> 23:28.060
Go and give Kamonohashi Ron a terrifying 
taste of the House of Moriarty.

23:24.380 --> 23:28.590
<b>Fourth-Born of the Moriarty Family
Winter Moriarty</b>
